# heap-probe.in -- stdin script for build-host/angband-test -mtest, run under
# LD_PRELOAD=heapshim.so by tools/host-build.sh. Reproduces the heap table in
# specifications.md section 7.1.
#
# One command per line; see specifications.md section 6.6. "key" pushes a keypress at the
# next TERM_XTRA_EVENT, so screen text lags a line behind the command that caused it; the
# depth? and heap? probes run immediately and are what the numbers are read from.
#
# The birth sequence is: space past the splash, 'a' for the first race, 'a' for the first
# class, 'a' to accept, then four returns through name, history and the final confirmation.
# The four "key ," after each jump are stand-still turns that let the game loop process the
# queued CMD_WIZ_JUMP_LEVEL and generate the new level.
#
# The jumps go 50, 30, 10, 98 -- shallow-to-deep with the deepest last, because a level-1
# character standing still on level 98 usually dies, and after death the game loop stops
# processing queued commands, so any jump after it silently reports the old depth.

heap? init

key space
key a
key a
key a
key enter
key enter
key enter
key enter

depth?
heap? town

jump 50
key ,
key ,
key ,
key ,
depth?
heap? L50

jump 30
key ,
key ,
key ,
key ,
depth?
heap? L30

jump 10
key ,
key ,
key ,
key ,
depth?
heap? L10

jump 98
key ,
key ,
key ,
key ,
depth?
heap? L98

quit
